    "['username [parameter1] password [parameter2] [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Cisco username configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A\\'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\"\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"super-user\" which is roughly equivalent to privilege level 3 in Cisco\\n2. The \"0\" in Cisco indicates cleartext password, but Juniper expects encrypted passwords by default\\n3. If you need to use the exact same cleartext password, you would use \"plain-text-password\" instead of \"encrypted-password\" in Juniper', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A\\'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\"', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A\\'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\"', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Cisco username configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A\\'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\"\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"super-user\" which is roughly equivalent to privilege level 3 in Cisco\\n2. The \"0\" in Cisco indicates cleartext password, but Juniper expects encrypted passwords by default\\n3. If you need to use the exact same cleartext password, you would use \"plain-text-password\" instead of \"encrypted-password\" in Juniper', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"@%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A\\'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\"'}]]"