    "['username [parameter1] privilege [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Cisco command `username client001 privilege 3` assigns privilege level 3 (which is typically equivalent to superuser/administrative privileges in Cisco) to the user \"client001\".\\n- In Juniper, the equivalent is assigning the \"super-user\" class to the user, which provides full administrative privileges.\\n- The Juniper command structure uses `set system login user <username> class <privilege-level>`.', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}]]": 1,
